msgctxt "@info"
msgid "The image contains pixels with zero alpha channel and non-zero color channels. Skissa has modified those pixels to have at least some alpha. The initial values will <i>not</i> be reverted on saving the image back.<br/><br/>This will hardly make any visual difference just keep it in mind."
msgstr "The image contains pixels with zero alpha channel and non-zero colour channels. Skissa has modified those pixels to have at least some alpha. The initial values will <i>not</i> be reverted on saving the image back.<br/><br/>This will hardly make any visual difference just keep it in mind."

msgctxt "@tooltip"
msgid "The image will be linearized first, and then encoded with SMPTE ST 428. Skissa always opens images like these as linear floating point, this option is there to reverse that"
msgstr "The image will be linearised first, and then encoded with SMPTE ST 428. Skissa always opens images like these as linear floating point, this option is there to reverse that"

msgid "Layer \"%1\" has blending mode \"%2\" that has changed its behavior for CMYK color in Krita 5.2. Please check the result and consider enabling legacy \"Additive\" algorithm in Settings->Configure Skissa->General->Tools->CMYK blending mode"
msgstr "Layer \"%1\" has blending mode \"%2\" that has changed its behaviour for CMYK colour in Skissa 5.2. Please check the result and consider enabling legacy \"Additive\" algorithm in Settings->Configure Skissa->General->Tools->CMYK blending mode"

msgid "The file is too new for this version of Skissa (%1)."
msgstr "The file is too new for this version of Skissa (%1)."

